# Implementation Plan: Cleaner Card Detail UI

The user found the red hero banner on the card detail page to be too overwhelming ("big red box"). This plan removes that banner and reintegrates the product information into a more balanced, professional white panel layout.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This change will remove the red gradient header. The card name and set information will move into the main white content area, similar to standard high-end e-commerce product pages.

## Proposed Changes

### [Component] Pokémon Card Detail View

#### [MODIFY] [view_card.php](file:///f:/UniServerZ/www/coolex_shop/application/views/store/view_card.php)
-   **CSS Cleanup:** Remove the `.card-page-hero` styles and its pseudo-elements (`::before`, `::after`).
-   **HTML Structure:** 
    - Delete the `card-page-hero` div (Lines 79-91).
    - Ensure the breadcrumb remains at the top for navigation.
    - Enhance the layout within the `product-container` so the card title and rarity feel integrated and premium without the external banner.
-   **Visual Polish:** Adjust padding and margins to ensure the transition from breadcrumb to product panel feels seamless.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Non-breaking UI change; no automated tests required. I will verify HTML tag balance.

### Manual Verification
- **Visual Check**: Open a Pokémon card page and verify the "big red box" is gone.
- **Layout Check**: Verify the card title, price, and "Add to Cart" button are still perfectly aligned and legible.
- **Functionality**: Ensure the quantity stepper and zoom still work perfectly.
